## Summary
Medium, Chill, and Easy bots now do a spread-first pass before picking by score percentile. This should stop them from endlessly piling plays on the right when the board already has a right-heavy cluster.

- `choose_move` now filters out the bottom 50% of legal plays by `spread_score` for `Medium`, `Chill`, and `Easy`.
- `spread_score` is the maximum Manhattan distance from any newly placed tile to the board's current tile center of mass.
- `Hard` and `Impossible` still pick from raw score percentiles.

```rust
// src/bot.rs
let center = tile_center(&game.board);
plays.sort_by_key(|play| std::cmp::Reverse(spread_score(center, &play.0)));
let spread_keep = (plays.len() * SPREAD_FILTER_PERCENT).div_ceil(100).max(1);
plays.truncate(spread_keep);
plays.sort_by_key(|play| std::cmp::Reverse(play.1.points));
```

The current filter keeps the top spreadiest 50% of plays; tune `SPREAD_FILTER_PERCENT` if needed.

